        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenji Mizoguchi, David Wall, Kōzaburō Yoshimura\n- Works: Noëlle, An Osaka Story\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, actor, producer\n- Events: Fort Lauderdale International Film Festival\n\nFacts:\n- Kenji Mizoguchi was a Japanese film director and screenwriter who was born on May 16, 1898, and died on August 24, 1956.\n- David Wall is an American actor who wrote, produced, and directed the 2007 dramedy film \"Noëlle\".\n- \"Noëlle\" won the Best Director Award at the Fort Lauderdale International Film Festival.\n- \"An Osaka Story\" is a 1957 black-and-white Japanese film directed by Kōzaburō Yoshimura.\n- \"An Osaka Story\" was based on a story by Kenji Mizoguchi.",
